aenigma (5.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  [ Romulus Ruja ]
  * New hub method Cleanup2 confirms pending messages up to a given id;
    Pull and Cleanup are deprecated in favor of Pull2 and Cleanup2. The
    bridge uses Cleanup2 and falls back to Cleanup for 5.0.x peers.
  * RouteMessage: a uuid must be a GUID and is allowed only with a single
    payload; it is stored in lowercase form. Relays must route one message
    per request, with its uuid.
  * PUT /IncrementSharedDataAccessCount and PUT /IncrementFileAccessCount
    answer 404 when no record has the given tag.
  * A new job removes expired and unlisted vertices from the graph every
    five minutes. New setting UnlistedVertexGracePeriod (default 00:06:00).
  * Every setting has a default; a value that cannot be read is replaced
    by its default and reported with a warning, at startup and when the
    configuration is reloaded.
  * A blacklist whose endpoint can never match is reported with a warning
    at startup.
  * The default log level of the package is Warning.
  * /etc/aenigma/appsettings.json is no longer a conffile. It holds only
    the settings that differ from the defaults in /usr/lib/aenigma, so an
    upgrade no longer stops at a configuration prompt and new defaults
    always apply. An existing file is reduced to its changed settings;
    the full file is kept as appsettings.json.dpkg-bak.
  * /var/log/aenigma has mode 750. New installations create the service
    user without a home directory, and a purge no longer tries to remove
    one.
  * Log properties renamed: CommendResult to CommandResult, and
    ConnectionIdKey to ConnectionId.
  * The dashboard state is kept by a single thread; a slow dashboard
    session no longer delays the others.
  * The background jobs page is available at /Jobs in the Development
    environment only.
  * Removed code that was never called and unused package references.

 -- Romulus-Emanuel Ruja <romulus.ruja@aenigma.ro>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 17:15:00 +0300

aenigma (5.0.1) unstable; urgency=high

  [ Romulus Ruja ]
  * Security: file tags are mapped to paths safely; GET /File could read
    files outside the upload directory.
  * Security: sign-in challenges come from a secure random source and can
    be used once.
  * Security: input lengths are checked before every call into libaenigma.
  * Security: the key passphrase is no longer written to the log.
  * Security: an Ephemeral passphrase is no longer kept in the persistent
    keyring; passphrases are handed to libaenigma zero-terminated.
  * Security: only nodes with a live session can become graph neighbors.
  * Security: /_blazor is blocked on the public endpoint by default;
    Newtonsoft.Json pinned to 13.0.3.
  * Cleanup confirms only messages the connection has pulled; Pull returns
    at most 128 messages. Fixes loss of pending messages.
  * Hub messages up to 331776 bytes are accepted, so batches of onions are
    no longer rejected; one onion may have at most 16384 characters.
  * Access counts and the duplicate uuid check are correct under
    concurrent requests.
  * Invalid or unknown input is answered with 400 or 404 instead of 500.
  * Missing retention settings default to the shipped values instead of 0.
  * The bridge signs in again after a peer restart, and stays quiet while
    the node's key is locked.
  * The dashboard works when started with run-prod.sh.
  * A failed file upload removes its record; a peer address can be stored
    only once.
  * aenigma-update is included in the package.

 -- Romulus-Emanuel Ruja <romulus.ruja@aenigma.ro>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 15:54:04 +0300

aenigma (5.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  [ Romulus Ruja ]
  * Core functionalities.

